\u003e-\n        The project's config file sets the greeting to a stated text\n        before the command runs.\n      terms: [greeting, command]\n  when:\n    - concept: a role runs a command\n      means: \u003e-\n        A role runs one stated command line once, in the project\n        directory, and waits for it to exit.\n      terms: [command]\n  then:\n    - concept: exit code\n      means: \u003e-\n        The command the role ran ended with a stated exit code; 0 means\n        it succeeded.\n      terms: [command, exit code]\n    - concept: standard output\n      means: \u003e-\n        One of the lines the command printed on its standard output, its\n        answer or a log record alike, has a match for a stated pattern, a\n        regular expression.\n      terms: [command, standard output]\n",
